subprocess/time, contextlib.contextmanager, collections.abc types) — since the moved bodies are byte-identical and reference these as globals.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.4,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["_store_git_op_lock body calls `logger.debug(...)` and `logger.warning(...)` (gitutil.py:347,358); _with_index_lock_retry calls `logger.debug` (gitutil.py:594)","Moved _is_index_lock_error returns `git_outcome.is_index_lock(text)` (gitutil.py:255) and _is_git_lock_error returns `git_outcome.is_git_lock(text)` (gitutil.py:267)","Plan lists only `_INDEX_LOCK_*`, `_STORE_GIT_LOCK_*`/`_FETCH_COORD_*`, `_LOCK_PATH_RE`/`_LOCK_REF_RE`, and the probes as state that travels — it does not mention `logger` or the `git_outcome` import for the new module"],"finding":"The plan's 'module-level state that MUST travel' list omits two runtime dependencies the moved bodies reference: the module-level `logger` (used by _store_git_op_lock, _with_index_lock_retry, fetch_coordination_lock, _acquire_fetch_coord_flock) and the `git_outcome` module import (used by the moved _is_index_lock_error / _is_git_lock_error via git_outcome.is_index_lock / is_git_lock). Since AC requires moved bodies byte-identical, git_locking.py must independently establish its own `logger = logging.getLogger(...)` and `import ... git_outcome` (plus `import fcntl/os/random/re/subprocess/time` and the contextlib/typing imports the moved functions use). The plan names only constants, regexes, and probes as things that travel, so as written the moved functions would raise NameError at runtime.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f71dc328027915eae","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"The seam — 'Module-level state the moved functions read as globals'","norm_id":"n2497f0c353e11aa9","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["First real call to run_git_write or fetch_coordination_lock under lock contention hits `logger` NameError in git_locking","Any lock-classification call raises NameError on `git_outcome` if the new module lacks the import"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Add `logger` and the `git_outcome` module import (plus the stdlib imports the moved functions use) to the list of things git_locking.py must define, and note that git_locking's own import block is constructed fresh (the 'differs only in docstring and import block' constraint applies to the RETAINED gitutil half, not the new module).","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Extend the test-consumer inventory with a fourth channel — direct `gitutil.<name>(...)` reads/calls — and for each moved-but-not-re-exported symbol read that way (`_lock_retry_budget_s` at test_git_contention_9305.py:151, `_store_git_lock_path` at :213, `_is_index_lock_error` at test_delete_init_index_lock.py:105 / test_compact_index_lock.py:87 / test_event_append_index_lock.py:121) either retarget the reference to `git_locking` or add a re-export, so no test moves from passing to failing.","cohort":["project.symbol-reference-completeness"],"criteria":["project.symbol-reference-completeness"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":0.0,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan (c): enumerates only `getattr(gitutil, \"_INDEX_LOCK_STALE_S\", 300)` reads and monkeypatch channels; it states probes/tunables are 'deliberately NOT re-exported'.","Re-export table lists ONLY production importers; `_lock_retry_budget_s`, `_store_git_lock_path`, `_is_index_lock_error` have none, so they are not re-exported.","tests/interfaces/store/test_git_contention_9305.py:151: `budget = gitutil._lock_retry_budget_s()` — direct call, not monkeypatch/getattr.","tests/interfaces/store/test_git_contention_9305.py:213: `fd = os.open(gitutil._store_git_lock_path(sys.argv[1]), ...)` in a subprocess script string — a moved, non-re-exported name.","tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_delete_init_index_lock.py:105 / test_compact_index_lock.py:87 / test_event_append_index_lock.py:121: `gitutil._is_index_lock_error(...)` — direct call on the module object."],"finding":"The test-consumer inventory omits a whole reference channel — direct attribute-access CALLS/READS of moved names as `gitutil.<name>(...)` — for three symbols that MOVE to git_locking and are NOT re-exported (no production importer, and probes/tunables 'deliberately NOT re-exported'): `_lock_retry_budget_s`, `_store_git_lock_path`, and `_is_index_lock_error`. The plan classifies its test consumers only under (a) monkeypatch.setattr, (b) reader-stayed monkeypatch, and (c) getattr-with-default, none of which cover a plain `gitutil._lock_retry_budget_s()` invocation.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f449f501e1b0b6811","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Section 'Test consumers, split by HOW they depend on a moved name' (categories (a)/(b)/(c)); re-export table under 'Re-exports gitutil must keep'","norm_id":"nee9b8fd176378d05","priority":0.9,"reason":"defau